From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:07:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: make the DDS loader state thread local

Can be submitted upstream: general engine fix.

ddsloader.cpp keeps the parsed header, the channel count and the bit shifts in file scope globals. Sprite
sheets are decoded on several loader threads at once, so two threads overwrote each other's m_dds between
Texture::Init (sized from one header) and internal_readimg (which re-reads the dimensions): squish wrote past
the end of the buffer and the process died with SIGSEGV in squish::DecompressImage (seen on Android with
STEINS;GATE's DXT5 system sheets, ten of them decoded within 30 ms).

Make the state thread_local; the functions are otherwise unchanged.

diff --git a/src/texture/ddsloader.cpp b/src/texture/ddsloader.cpp
index 7810919e3d7a3cdbc1ea5ef62ba41020e6f87f26..621184d1379db51e38dca54c369869500245e9e6 100644
--- a/src/texture/ddsloader.cpp
+++ b/src/texture/ddsloader.cpp
@@ -103,15 +103,18 @@ typedef struct {
   dds_caps caps;      ///< DirectDraw Surface caps
 } dds_header;
 
-std::vector<uint8_t> m_buf;  ///< Buffer the image pixels
-int m_nchans;                ///< Number of colour channels in image
-int m_nfaces;                ///< Number of cube map sides in image
-int m_Bpp;                   ///< Number of bytes per pixel
-int m_redL, m_redR;          ///< Bit shifts to extract red channel
-int m_greenL, m_greenR;      ///< Bit shifts to extract green channel
-int m_blueL, m_blueR;        ///< Bit shifts to extract blue channel
-int m_alphaL, m_alphaR;      ///< Bit shifts to extract alpha channel
-dds_header m_dds;
+// Textures are decoded from several loader threads at once, so this state must not be shared between them: with
+// plain globals two threads overwrote each other's header and one decoded past the end of its buffer (SIGSEGV in
+// squish::DecompressImage while a profile loaded its sprite sheets).
+thread_local std::vector<uint8_t> m_buf;  ///< Buffer the image pixels
+thread_local int m_nchans;                ///< Number of colour channels in image
+thread_local int m_nfaces;                ///< Number of cube map sides in image
+thread_local int m_Bpp;                   ///< Number of bytes per pixel
+thread_local int m_redL, m_redR;          ///< Bit shifts to extract red channel
+thread_local int m_greenL, m_greenR;      ///< Bit shifts to extract green channel
+thread_local int m_blueL, m_blueR;        ///< Bit shifts to extract blue channel
+thread_local int m_alphaL, m_alphaR;      ///< Bit shifts to extract alpha channel
+thread_local dds_header m_dds;
 
 inline void calc_shifts(int mask, int& left, int& right) {
   if (mask == 0) {
